<code>assert index >= 0 && index < \old(this.size()) => \forall int i; index < i && i < \old(this.size()); this.get(i) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null ? null : \old(this.get(i+1)));</code>
--------------------
<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size()); (this.get(i) == null) == (\old(this.get(i+1)) == null) && (this.get(i) != null => this.get(i).equals(\old(this.get(i+1))));</code>

However, since we need to ensure that the element at position `i` after the operation is either null if the old element at position `i+1` was null, or it equals the old element at position `i+1`, we can simplify the assertion as follows:

<code>assert \forall int i; index<i && i<\old(this.size()); this.get(i) == \old(this.get(i+1));</code>

This captures the essence that each element from the position `index+1` to the end of the vector is shifted down by one position.
